resources.string:
Pisar uses the accessibility service to:

• show the microphone button when a text field is open;
• notice that you hold volume down in a text field;
• put the dictated text where the cursor is.

For this, Pisar sees which text field is open and what is written in it. It does not store any of it and sends it nowhere. Speech is recognized on the phone. Only if you turn on the cloud Brain yourself does the dictated text go to the service you chose; the Brain never works in password fields.
